<comment type="function">
<text evidence="3">Bacteriocin active against Gram-positive bacteria. Inhibits B.cereus spore outgrowth, after the germination stage, approximately 1000-fold better than it inhibits exponential growth of the same cells. Inhibits B.subtilis strain ATCC 6633.</text>
</comment>
<comment type="subunit">
<text>Monomer.</text>
</comment>
<comment type="subcellular location">
<subcellularLocation>
<location evidence="3">Secreted</location>
</subcellularLocation>
<text>Extracellular region.</text>
</comment>
<comment type="PTM">
<text>Production of active sublancin-168 requires at least one thiol-disulfide oxidoreductase (BdbB or, in its absence, BdbC). Membrane translocation and cleavage of the precursor are probably performed by SunT.</text>
</comment>
